<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ w.file_name }}: Redshift migration assessment</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1f2a44; --muted: #5b6577; --line: #d9dee7; --wash: #f3f5f8; --paper: #ffffff;
    --high: #b02a37; --high-bg: #f8d7da; --med: #8a6508; --med-bg: #fff3cd;
    --low: #2e7d4f; --low-bg: #d1e7dd; --none-bg: #e9ecef;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink);
         font: 16px/1.6 "IBM Plex Sans", "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 64px; background: var(--paper); }
  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 4px; font-weight: 600; word-break: break-word; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 48px 0 12px; font-weight: 600; }
  h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 4px; font-weight: 600; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; max-width: 72ch; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  a { color: var(--ink); }
  a:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #4c7bd9; outline-offset: 2px; }

  /* The score scale: the one bold element */
  .scale { margin: 8px 0 8px; }
  .scale-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .scale-num { font-size: 3.2rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .scale-num span { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  .scale-band { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .segments { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr); gap: 3px; }
  .seg { height: 14px; background: var(--wash); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .seg.on.low { background: var(--low); border-color: var(--low); }
  .seg.on.medium { background: #c99a1a; border-color: #c99a1a; }
  .seg.on.high { background: var(--high); border-color: var(--high); }
  .ticks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr); color: var(--muted);
           font-size: .75rem; margin-top: 4px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .facts { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 10px; }

  .summary { font-size: 1.08rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--ink); padding-left: 16px; }
  .ai-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }

  .ref { display: inline-block; font-size: .78em; font-weight: 600; padding: 0 5px; margin: 0 1px;
         border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; background: var(--wash); white-space: nowrap; }

  .diagram { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 16px; }
  .diagram pre.mermaid { margin: 0; min-width: 640px; }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 8px; }
  .legend i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: -1px; border: 1px solid #999; }

  .risk { border-left: 4px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 0 4px 14px; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .risk.high { border-color: var(--high); } .risk.medium { border-color: #c99a1a; } .risk.low { border-color: var(--low); }
  .sev { font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 3px; margin-left: 6px; vertical-align: 2px; }
  .sev.high { background: var(--high-bg); color: var(--high); }
  .sev.medium { background: var(--med-bg); color: var(--med); }
  .sev.low { background: var(--low-bg); color: var(--low); }
  .sev.none { background: var(--none-bg); color: var(--muted); }

  ol.steps { padding-left: 1.4em; } ol.steps li { margin-bottom: 8px; max-width: 72ch; }
  ul.parts { list-style: none; padding: 0; } ul.parts li { margin-bottom: 8px; }

  details { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 12px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 12px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
  code { font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", Consolas, monospace; font-size: .85em; word-break: break-word; }

  .callout { background: var(--wash); padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0; }
  footer { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  footer p { max-width: none; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) { main { padding: 24px 16px 48px; } .scale-num { font-size: 2.6rem; } }
  @media print { body { background: none; } main { padding: 0; } details { display: block; } .diagram { overflow: visible; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>{{ w.file_name }}</h1>
  <p class="sub">Redshift migration assessment{% if w.kind == "macro" %} of a macro{% endif %}, generated {{ generated }}</p>

  <section class="scale" aria-label="Difficulty score {{ s.score }} out of 10">
    <div class="scale-head">
      <div class="scale-num">{{ s.score }}<span>/10</span></div>
      <div class="scale-band">{{ band }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="segments">
      {% for i in range(1, 11) %}<div class="seg {% if i <= s.score %}on {{ level }}{% endif %}"></div>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="ticks">{% for i in range(1, 11) %}<span>{{ i }}</span>{% endfor %}</div>
    <p class="facts">{{ tool_count }} tools, {{ s.total_points }} difficulty points:
      {{ s.difficulty_counts.high }} high, {{ s.difficulty_counts.medium }} medium, {{ s.difficulty_counts.low }} low.
      {{ g.findings | length }} migration gotchas found.</p>
  </section>

  {% if macros %}
  <div class="callout">This workflow calls {% for m in macros %}<a href="{{ m.link }}">{{ m.file }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Its logic is in a separate file and is assessed in its own report.</div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>In short</h2>
  {% if ai %}
    <p class="summary">{{ refs(ai.summary) }}</p>
    <p class="ai-note">Written by AI ({{ ai._check.model }}) from facts extracted by code. Every tool it cites was checked against the workflow.</p>
  {% else %}
    <p>The AI summary hasn't been generated for this workflow yet.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>How data flows</h2>
  <div class="diagram"><pre class="mermaid">{{ mermaid }}</pre></div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i style="background:#f8d7da"></i>High difficulty</span>
    <span><i style="background:#fff3cd"></i>Medium</span>
    <span><i style="background:#d1e7dd"></i>Low</span>
    <span><i style="background:#e9ecef"></i>Nothing to migrate</span>
  </div>

  {% if ai %}
  <h2>Main risks</h2>
  {% for r in ai.risks %}
    <div class="risk {{ r.severity }}">
      <h3>{{ r.title }}<span class="sev {{ r.severity }}">{{ r.severity }}</span></h3>
      <p>{{ refs(r.detail) }}</p>
    </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ol class="steps">{% for step in ai.next_steps %}<li>{{ refs(step) }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>

  <h2>What the workflow does</h2>
  <ul class="parts">{% for k in ai.key_components %}
    <li>{% for t in k.tools %}{{ ref_chip(t) }}{% endfor %} {{ k.description }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Details</h2>
  <details>
    <summary>Every tool and its Redshift equivalent ({{ tool_count }})</summary>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it does</th><th>Difficulty</th><th>In Redshift</th></tr>
      {% for t in tools %}
      <tr><td>{{ t.name }} <span class="ref">{{ t.tool_id }}</span></td><td>{{ t.does }}</td>
          <td><span class="sev {{ t.difficulty }}">{{ t.difficulty }}</span></td><td>{{ t.redshift or "" }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Every gotcha found ({{ gotcha_groups | length }} kinds, {{ g.findings | length }} in total)</summary>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Issue</th><th>Tools</th><th>Evidence</th><th>What to do in Redshift</th></tr>
      {% for x in gotcha_groups %}
      <tr><td><span class="sev {{ x.severity }}">{{ x.severity }}</span><br>{{ x.message }}</td>
          <td>{% for t in x.tools %}<span class="ref">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{% for e in x.evidence %}<code>{{ e }}</code><br>{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{{ x.redshift }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </details>

  <footer>
    <p>How this report was made: code read the workflow file, scored each tool against editable rules (tool_rules.yaml), and checked formulas and settings for known migration issues (formula_gotchas.yaml). The AI only explains those facts. The score is the rules' output, not the AI's opinion.</p>
    <p>Limits: the analyzer reads workflow logic, not data. Data-dependent issues, such as a date format that doesn't match the actual data, are flagged as risks to test rather than detected directly. Effort and cost aren't estimated.</p>
  </footer>
</main>
<script type="module">
  import mermaid from "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs";
  mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: true, theme: "base", themeVariables: { fontFamily: "IBM Plex Sans, Segoe UI, sans-serif", lineColor: "#5b6577", edgeLabelBackground: "#f3f5f8" } });
</script>
</body>
</html>
